Use the NVL function to replace a NULL value with a specified replacement value.
- NVL syntax: SELECT NVL('CN/EXPRESSION','REPLACE VALUE') FROM TN;
- NVL replaces NULL with the provided value in a single column.
- Example: SELECT NVL(COMM, '100') AS COMMISSION FROM EMP;
- NVL can be used with all columns: SELECT EMP.*, NVL(COMM,'100') AS COMMISSION FROM EMP;
- NVL2 replaces both NULL and non-NULL values with different specified values.
- NVL2 syntax: SELECT NVL2('CN/EXPRESSION','NOTNULL VLAUE','NULL VLAUE');
- NVL2 example: SELECT EMP.*, NVL2(COMM,'5000','2000') FROM EMP;
